<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Form W-9</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  td { padding: 4px 0; }
  .section-header { font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 18pt;">Form W-9</h1>
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt;">(Massachusetts Substitute W-9)</h2>
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt;">Rev. March 2020</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <p>Completed form should be</p>
      <p>given to the requesting</p>
      <p>department or the department</p>
      <p>you are currently doing</p>
      <p>business with.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p>Name (as shown on your income tax return). Name is required on this line, do not leave this line blank.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <label>Business name/disregarded entity name, if different from above.</label>
      <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; margin-top: 2px;">
        <span data-field="business_name">{{ business_name }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p>Check the appropriate box:</p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
      <label><input type="checkbox"> Individual/Sole proprietor or single-member LLC</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox"> C Corporation</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox"> S Corporation</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox"> Partnership</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox"> Trust/Estate</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox"> Other</label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p>Legal Address: ____________________________________________________________________</p>
    <p>Remittance Address: If different from legal address number, street, apt. or suite no</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p>City, state and ZIP code _________________________</p>
    <p>City, state and ZIP code _________________________</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Phone: _________________________</td>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Fax: _________________________</td>
        <td style="width: 40%;">Email address: _________________________</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">Part I Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN)</h3>
    <p>Enter your TIN in the appropriate box. For individuals, this is your social security number (SSN). However, for a resident alien, this is your TIN as a disregarded entity, see the Part I instruction on page 2. For other entities, it is your employer identification number (EIN). If you do not have a number, see how to get a TIN on page 2.</p>
    <p>Note: If the account is in more than one name, see the chart on page 2 for guidelines on whose number to enter.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 50%;">Vendors:</td>
        <td style="width: 50%;">DUNS</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding-top: 5px;">Dunn and Bradstreet Universal Numbering System (DUNS)</td>
        <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; width: 50%;"></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">Part II Certification</h3>
    <p>Under penalties of perjury, I certify that:</p>
    <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>The number shown on this form is my correct taxpayer identification number (or I am waiting for a number to be issued to me), and</li>
      <li>I am not subject to backup withholding because I am exempt from backup withholding, or</li>
      <li>I am subject to backup withholding as a result of a failure to report all interest or dividends, or (c) the IRS has notified me that I am no longer subject to backup withholding, and</li>
      <li>I am an U.S. person (including an U.S. resident alien).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Certification instructions: You must cross out item 2 above if you have been notified by the IRS that you are currently subject to backup withholding because you have failed to report all interest and dividends on your tax return. For real estate transactions, item 2 does not apply.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
      <p>Sign _________________________ Date _________________________</p>
      <p>Here _________________________ Authorized Signature _________________________</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">Purpose of Form</h3>
      <p>A person who is required to file an information return with the IRS and who is subject to backup taxpayer identification number (TIN) to report, for example, interest, dividends, rents, royalties, or other payments, to you, real estate transactions, mortgage interest paid, or other payments, to you made by you.</p>
      <p>Use Form W-9 only if you are a U.S. person (including a resident alien), to give your correct TIN to the requesting (that is, the payer) and, when applicable, to:</p>
      <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Certify that you are not subject to backup withholding, and</li>
        <li>If you are a foreign person, use the form W-8BEN or W-8BEN-E. See Pub. 515 for withholding of tax on nonresident aliens and foreign corporations.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>What is backup withholding? Persons making certain payments to you must withhold a percentage of the payment and pay to the IRS of such payments under certain</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">How to get a TIN.</h3>
      <p>If you do not have a TIN, apply for one immediately. To apply for an individual, you must apply for a Social Security Card, from your local Social Security Administration office. Get Form W-9, Application for Tax Identification Number, or apply for an ITIN from Form SS-4. Or, apply for an EIN from the IRS's Internet Site Web www.irs.gov.</p>
      <p>If you do not have a TIN, write "Applied For" in the space for the TIN sign, and date the form, and mail it to the requesting payer. If you are a partnership, and certain payments made with this form are taxable interest, dividends, rents, royalties, or other payments, you will receive not be subject to backup withholding. Payments you receive will be subject to backup withholding.</p>
      <p>1. You do not furnish your TIN to the requesting payer.</p>
      <p>2. You do not certify that you WHEN required (see the Part II instructions on page 2 for details).</p>
      <p>The IRS tells you that you are subject to backup withholding because you did not report all interest and dividends only, or</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div style="width: 48%;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">Penalties</h3>
        <p>Failure to furnish a TIN. If you fail to furnish your TIN to the requesting payer, you are subject to a penalty of $20 for each such failure unless your TIN is exempt from backup withholding.</p>
        <p>Civil penalty for false information with respect to backup withholding. If you make a false statement with no reasonable basis that results in no backup withholding, you are subject to a $500 penalty.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 48%;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 12pt;">Give the Requestor</h3>
        <p>For this type of account:</p>
        <table style="width: 100%;">
          <tr>
            <td style="width: 50%;">Give name and SSN of:</td>
            <td style="width: 50%;"></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Individual</td>
            <td>The owner of the account, if combined</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Corporation</td>
            <td>The individual on the account</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Partnership</td>
            <td>The owner</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Trust/Estate</td>
            <td>The minor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Other</td>
            <td>The grantor's trustee</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <p style="margin-top: 15px;">For this type of account:</p>
        <table style="width: 100%;">
          <tr>
            <td style="width: 50%;">Give name and EIN of:</td>
            <td style="width: 50%;"></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Corporation</td>
            <td>The corporation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Partnership</td>
            <td>The partnership</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Trust/Estate</td>
            <td>The grantor's trustee</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="checkbox"> Other</td>
            <td>The public entity</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>